\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Top Level: This level has the highest amount of sunlight in the whole tank, only accessible by the most wealthy, and only the extremely important people live here. It includes personal houses with beautiful views of the ocean and great quality of life.
\f0\fs24 \
\

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 Upper Residences: An exclusive area where higher ups live in the built-in living quarters. Here, we can find officials and some of the higher class citizens of the tank. It includes the best schools and offers some of the best quality of life accessible by a normal citizen.
\f0\fs24 \
\

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 Market Levels: An upper-middle class area made up of the best supermarkets with the highest quality produce are found, mainly meant for high class citizens, but accessible by everyone. It also includes sparse living quarters throughout the level.
\f0\fs24 \
\

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 Middle levels: average people live here, there are some stores throughout it, like Torin\'92s, there is some sunlight, you can sometimes hear the low rumble of the engine, the archimedes school holds more students than any of the other two in the tank, including Mira and Ocean, also The Curie institute of health, were citizens of the lower levels are sent when they are really sick.
\f0\fs24 \
\

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 Lower levels: almost non-existent sunlight, people with \'91easy\'92 jobs live here, it is extremely warm and damp because of its proximity to the engine room, this is also where all of the factories are located, so it\'92s very loud during the day. There are no shops or commodities, only a very underprivileged and low funded school and hospital. The residences are very small and cramped, and in overall very poor conditions.
\f0\fs24 \
